cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it."
title: "Timeframe Is a Parameter, Not a Truth: A Pre-Registered, Cost-Aware Evaluation of Trading Signals"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered evaluation of 1,008 timeframe-dependent trading strategies
  on Binance 1-minute and 5-minute data and EODHD daily equities, spanning
  six decision timeframes from 5 minutes to 1 day. The study tests claims
  about volatility scaling, multi-timeframe filters, transaction-cost drag,
  backtest overfitting, budget-constrained timeframe choice, and live
  multi-venue signal agreement. The best in-sample strategy fails out of
  sample, higher-timeframe filters reduce risk and turnover without adding
  much gross alpha, and cost drag rises by orders of magnitude at short
  horizons.
authors:
  - name: "Timeframe Validity Project"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-21
license: MIT
type: software
keywords:
  - timeframe analysis
  - multiple timeframes
  - transaction costs
  - backtest overfitting
  - market microstructure
  - reproducibility
